<title>JAPAN: Cosmo Oil to import Japan's first Eocene crude.</title>
<headline>Cosmo Oil to import Japan's first Eocene crude.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cosmo Oil Co Ltd said on Tuesday it had signed a contract with U.S. oil major Texaco Inc to import 300,000 barrels of Eocene crude, which is produced in the Neutral Zone between Kuwait and Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>The Eocene imports will be the first to Japan since Kuwait Oil Company and Texaco began commercial production in the Wafra oil field in October 1996, Cosmo Oil said in a statement.</p>
<p>The crude, to be used to produce asphalt, will be loaded between April 15 and 30 at the Gulf port of Mina Saud and will be shipped to Cosmo Oil's Yokkaichi refinery in central Japan, the statement said.</p>
<p>Eocene crude is of 18 degrees API (American Petroleum Institute) gravity and has a sulphur content of 3.62 percent, the statement said.</p>
</text>
